<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	The Mac Catalyst build only — project.yml attaches this with an
	[sdk=macosx*] condition, because neither key means anything on iOS, where
	the app is sandboxed unconditionally and may open outgoing connections
	without asking.

	Both keys are load-bearing on the Mac. A Catalyst app must adopt the App
	Sandbox, and a sandboxed app with no network-client entitlement cannot open
	an outgoing connection at all — so the app would launch, look entirely
	healthy, and fail every request to the user's server with what appears to
	be an unreachable-host error. That is the failure this file prevents, and
	it is not one the iOS build can ever reproduce.

	Nothing else is granted. Reading files the user picks, and the incoming
	connections a future Cast bridge might want, are separate entitlements to
	be added when the phase that needs them arrives.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
